  "title": "Claude consultant seat cannot start \u2014 ACP session lost and startup handshake times out (DIG-628 outage)",
  "description": "The Claude seat is failing to run. DIG-628 has been `in_progress` since 2026-10-05 01:05 with **zero work produced** after 2.5 hours. All three comments on that issue are infrastructure failures, not agent output.\n\n**Exact errors, verbatim:**\n\n1. `Persistent ACP session 7a113b9a-2675-42f5-8f04-bbfab58e82a1 could not be resumed: Resource not found: 7a113b9a-2675-42f5-8f04-bbfab58e82a1` (twice)\n2. `The ACP startup handshake did not finish before the startup deadline.`\n\n**What this looks like.** A stale persistent-session pointer: the seat is trying to resume ACP session `7a113b9a-...`, which no longer exists, and the handshake then never completes before the deadline. That is an adapter/session-state fault, not a model or prompt fault.\n\n**Why it matters beyond this one job.** The Claude Pro seat is the **only** working consultant seat right now:\n- **Cursor** premium allowance was exhausted on 2026-10-04 (Opus 5 refused).\n- **OpenCode Go** is OFF and stays off until Chris says he logged back in.\n\nThere is no step-down available to another consultant seat. It is also blocking a second thing: the Claude Pro weekly usage meter has been **unmeasured** since the budget was set up, and `/us\n\n[truncated, 2041 characters total; open the issue for the full brief]",
