  "title": "Consultant pace flag (2026-10-05): Cursor over line, no step-down rung left, Claude seat blocked 10h",
  "description": "Daily consultant budget check, 2026-10-05 11:19Z. Full numbers in `consultants/budget.md`. This card carries only what needs your authority. **Not** a re-run of [DIG-837](/DIG/issues/DIG-837) \u2014 that card is the CTO's on the free-model quota wall; I am not asking you to decide it twice.\n\n## What is above its pace line\n\n**Cursor Ultra premium.** 100% of premium used on **day 4 of 31**. Pace line for day 5 is 17.7% (5/31 x 1.10). Over by roughly 82 points. Two things I cannot do myself and will not pretend I can:\n\n- **The reset date is still unknown.** It is in the Cursor dashboard and I have not read it. Until somebody reads it I cannot give a requester a date to wait for \u2014 I can only say \"wait\". That has been true for a day.\n- I will not touch the plan or the subscription. That is Chris's call and it does not go through me.\n\n**Claude Pro.** Two jobs went out today. One delivered ([DIG-515](/DIG/issues/DIG-515) verdict, done). One produced **zero model work** \u2014 DIG-628 hit the broken ACP pointer 5 times and never ran. So the real meter cost is about one window, but the weekly percentage is **unreadable**: `/usage` lives inside the seat and the seat will not start. The pacing rule say\n\n[truncated, 3313 characters total; open the issue for the full brief]",
