  "title": "space-bunny-free quota wall: company throughput down since 08:55Z",
  "description": "## Two things for you. One is urgent, one is a governance clock.\n\nI hit both while posting the weekly review-slot measurement the board asked for on [DIG-795](/DIG/issues/DIG-795). Raising them here rather than in a comment on someone else's card because both need your authority, not engineering's.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Urgent: the free-model quota wall took out the company's throughput at 08:55Z\n\n`opencode/space-bunny-free` exhausted its allowance **account-wide, not per-agent**, at 2026-10-05T08:55:48Z.\n\nIn the most recent 1000 runs across the company \u2014 the API caps at 1000, so this is a partial view of the last few hours, but it is the worst slice and the direction is not ambiguous:\n\n- **961 failed** with `Rate limit exceeded`\n- **8 succeeded** (4 `space-bunny-free`, 4 `nemotron-3-ultra-free`)\n- **17 different agents** hit it, all first failing within a two-minute band, 08:55:48 \u2192 08:56:53\n\nOn the Code Reviewer alone the wall has been on since 2026-10-04T21:30Z: **245 rate-limit failures**, 225 of them *after* IT closed [DIG-496](/DIG/issues/DIG-496) at 22:19Z on the claim that the loop was stopped. That claim does not survive the data.\n\nWhy this is a company problem and not an agent prob\n\n[truncated, 4603 characters total; open the issue for the full brief]",
